    "reason": "Owner explicitly requested local hindsight-embed daemon with Codex-backed native memory instead of Docker on 2026-11-15. Reviewed-record bank remains separate and chunk-only. Review-runner children disable native memory hooks/MCP to preserve independent read-only review isolation. The standalone plan-review recipe and native architecture role also require an isolated parent/process. Owner switched the Codex model from gpt-6.1-sol to gpt-6.2-sol on 2026-11-18 (live call confirmed access); the routing policy, runner, validator, doctor text, Codex roles, plan-review recipe and model references in reference/skills docs carry that local model pin. Efforts and gates unchanged. Fresh reviews run in a disposable copy-on-write clone of the checkout with a private temp folder (policy/review-sandbox.json, read from the task's base commit), so they can run every project check while the real checkout, run folder and shared temp stay read-only; the user Codex config (and its MCP servers) is not loaded; the turn's processes are killed and the clone deleted afterwards; repair turns are pinned to the real checkout with -C. Network is on (accepted risk; owner decision 2026-11-18).",
